<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>NYT &gt; Technology</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/section/technology</link><description>Technology industry news, commentary, and analysis, with reporting on big tech, startups, and internet culture. The New York Times is a hub for conversation about news and ideas.</description><atom:link rel="self" href="https://rss.nytimes.com/services/xml/rss/nyt/Technology.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>Spotify Will Label A.I. Artists and Avoid Promoting Them</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/11/arts/music/spotify-artificial-intelligence-music.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/11/arts/music/spotify-artificial-intelligence-music.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/11/arts/music/spotify-artificial-intelligence-music.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The new label, which will begin to be applied next month, is an effort by the streaming service to be more transparent about A.I.-generated music on its app.</description><dc:creator>Malia Mendez</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 19:00:55 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Music</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Spotify</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Product Labels</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Audio Recordings</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Downloads and Streaming</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/11/multimedia/11cul-spotify-ai-03-wcvj/11cul-spotify-ai-03-wcvj-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>via Spotify</media:credit><media:description>Spotify said its review process would involve an automated screening followed by a check from the company’s human moderators. Users will be able to appeal the designation.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>How Social Media Sparked a Refugee Crisis Between Spain and Morocco</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/11/technology/social-media-ceuta-spain-morocco.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/11/technology/social-media-ceuta-spain-morocco.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/11/technology/social-media-ceuta-spain-morocco.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>A wave of disinformation online contributed to a surge of migrants in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta who were trying to reach Europe, resulting in about 90 deaths.</description><dc:creator>Steven Lee Myers, Aida Alami and Carlos Barragán</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:03:41 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Migrant Surge into Ceuta</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Spain</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Migrant Surge into Spanish Territory</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Ceuta Spain</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Social Media</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Illegal Immigration</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Undocumented Migrants</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Refugees</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Internally Displaced People</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Decisions and Verdicts</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Rumors and Misinformation</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Human trafficking</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Facebook</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Instagram</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Meta</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Telegram</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">TikTok</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">WhatsApp</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/09/multimedia/00biz-ceuta-disinfo-1-wgjt/00biz-ceuta-disinfo-1-wgjt-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Sergey Ponomarev for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>Moroccan border guards and boats patrolling the coastline on the border with Spain in Fnideq, Morocco, this month.</media:description></media:content></item></channel></rss>